a9d11344a66b2d6a0da557272bd721","message":"Writer: keep a dynamic PIE's calls of __tls_get_addr that no access makes (#511's review)\n\n#521 made the writer treat every fixup to __tls_get_addr in a dynamic PIE\nas a general- or local-dynamic access's call, and refused the link when\nthose calls outnumbered the accesses. A program that calls the loader's\nfunction itself, with a tls_index of its own, was linked as an import\nbefore #521 and is again: only a call whose fixup follows a TLSGD or TLSLD\nfixup (executable_relaxed_call's rule) is consumed by the relaxation. The\ncount marks no slot or stub for those, and every other call marks them as\nany import's. A static executable, where nothing defines the function,\nstill refuses such a call.\n\ntest-dynamic replaces the refusal it expected with a PIE that calls\n__tls_get_addr through its stub and its GOT slot with the executable's own\nmodule, beside a relaxed access, written on every lane count and by the\nexact twins, compared with lld's link and run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013JQmU9xdZeki1dFKkhvRm2\nSigned-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-27T10:55:35Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1421805693,"node_id":"R_kgDOVL8IfQ","name":"buster","full_name":"buster14a/buster","private":false,"owner":{"login":"buster14a","id":139068652,"node_id":"O_kgDOCEoE7A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139068652?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a","html_url":"https://github.com/buster14a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster1